# Implementation Plan: Generalized Bearing Fault Model Retraining & Autonomous Auto-Fit Inference System

## Goal Description
1. Retrain and generalize the bearing fault prediction models using the provided CWRU dataset (`CWRU_dataset/raw/data/*.xlsx` and `CWRU_48k_load_1_CNN_data.npz` / `.xlsx`).
2. Implement data augmentation (circular shift, Gaussian noise perturbation, amplitude scaling) and an upgraded 1D CNN architecture (multi-scale feature extraction, residual skip connections, batch normalization, and dropout) for robust, high-efficiency, generalized inference.
3. Replace the manual model selection UI dropdown with an **Autonomous Model Selection Engine** where the system dynamically analyzes the input signal characteristics (SNR, crest factor, kurtosis, softmax entropy, model certainty) to determine and execute the best-fit model automatically.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Model Retraining & Generalization Pipeline
#### [MODIFY] [preprocess.py](file:///c:/workshop-maintenance-system/ml/preprocessing/preprocess.py)
- Support data ingestion from `CWRU_dataset/raw/data` (10 raw accelerometer files with 485k+ samples each) as well as the 1024-window benchmark (`CWRU_48k_load_1_CNN_data.npz` / `.xlsx`).
- Add data augmentation routines for signal generalization:
  - Random circular phase shift (simulating varying vibration sensor starting points).
  - Additive Gaussian noise (simulating industrial plant electrical and background noise at varying SNRs).
  - Mild amplitude scaling (0.9x – 1.1x).
- Ensure canonical feature scaler and label encoders are fitted strictly on the leakage-safe training split.

#### [MODIFY] [train_cnn.py](file:///c:/workshop-maintenance-system/ml/training/train_cnn.py)
- Upgrade the 1D Deep CNN architecture to a Generalized Residual Multi-Scale 1D CNN:
  - Large receptive field initial layer (kernel size 64) for low-frequency shaft harmonics.
  - Residual skip connections with Batch Normalization and Spatial Dropout to prevent overfitting.
  - Global Average Pooling + dense classification head with L2 regularization.
- Train with early stopping, learning rate scheduling on plateau, and augmented batches.
- Output benchmark evaluations, confusion matrix, and training curves.
- Save best model checkpoints to `ml/saved_models/cnn_cwru_1024_v1.keras` and `cnn_model.keras`.

#### [MODIFY] [train_ml.py](file:///c:/workshop-maintenance-system/ml/training/train_ml.py)
- Retrain classical models (Random Forest, SVM, Gradient Boosting) on canonical 1024-sample features.
- Calibrate probabilities and export evaluation artifacts.

